35171.4 gpu: world feature feature=bumpmap declared=25 visible=25 resolved=25 missing=0 first=METAL/METALDOOR001 resource=materials/Metal/metaldoor001_normal.vtf reason=the materials name 17 distinct $bumpmap textures, so the one sampler slot the pass started with cannot apply each material's own; per-material binding is the --world-material-bump switch, and with it on the 14 that do not set $ssbump sample their own tile through a texinfo-axis tangent basis while the 11 that do stay refused (see the $ssbump row)
35171.4 gpu: world feature feature=bumpmap2 declared=0 visible=0 resolved=0 missing=0 first=- resource=- reason=-
35171.4 gpu: world feature feature=ssbump declared=17 visible=17 resolved=11 missing=6 first=WINTER/BLENDGRAVELTOGRASS_BAGEL resource=Metal/wall011d_bump-ssbump reason=$ssbump selects `BUMPMAP == 2`, where the texel is not a signed normal but three bumpBasis weights against three lightmap directions; this pass samples one lightmap and one tangent-space normal, so these materials are refused by name even when --world-material-bump is on
35171.4 gpu: world feature feature=detail declared=19 visible=19 resolved=0 missing=19 first=WOOD/WOOD_FLOOR002 resource=materials/overlays/detail006.vmt reason=detail layers are the --world-detail switch: the detail material's $basetexture is sampled at the atlas uv scaled by $detailscale and combined with the albedo by $detailblendmode; with the switch off the layer is refused
